      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A fifty-one year old man on chronic steroid therapy presented with a cellulitis-erysipelas-like eruption which proved to be histoplasmosis without demonstrable systemic involvement. This presentation deviates from the five previously reported cases, two nodular and three noduloulcerative, all of which presented as a self-limited, minimally tender lesion."},
